        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 199.05,
          "end": 202.2,
          "en": "Again, the same data, but in the XML format.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 202.2,
          "end": 203.46,
          "en": "Now, if you look at the formats,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 203.46,
          "end": 205.47,
          "en": "of course, JSON looks better than XML,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 205.47,
          "end": 206.82,
          "en": "but let's say if you have an application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 206.82,
          "end": 209.01,
          "en": "where you just want to consume XML,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 209.01,
          "end": 210.03,
          "en": "then you don't have a choice, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 210.03,
          "end": 212.07,
          "en": "You have to use XML format there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 212.07,
          "end": 215.7,
          "en": "So, this works, but what if you have one more restriction,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 215.7,
          "end": 219.66,
          "en": "that from the server side, only JSON should go.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 219.66,
          "end": 222.72,
          "en": "You don't want your client to accept XML.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 222.72,
          "end": 224.52,
          "en": "One way you can remove the library.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 224.52,
          "end": 227.25,
          "en": "Or, when you turn the data here, you can also mention",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 227.25,
          "end": 230.67000000000002,
          "en": "that this particular method will only work with JSON.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 230.67000000000002,
          "end": 231.503,
          "en": "Can we do that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 231.503,
          "end": 233.85,
          "en": "Can we negotiate a content whereby,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 233.85,
          "end": 237.57,
          "en": "by saying, let's only send JSON, let's not send XML.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 237.57,
          "end": 239.34,
          "en": "The way you do that is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 239.34,
          "end": 240.78,
          "en": "I mean, of course, you cannot specify",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 240.78,
          "end": 242.64,
          "en": "that you don't want to send XML,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 242.64,
          "end": 245.19,
          "en": "but you can specify what you want to send.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 245.19,
          "end": 248.4,
          "en": "So, first of all, which was the default path,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 248.4,
          "end": 251.91,
          "en": "let's mention the variable name path there, give a comma,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 251.91,
          "end": 254.82,
          "en": "and you can say it'll only produce,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 254.82,
          "end": 256.74,
          "en": "in the curly brackets, you can mention,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 256.74,
          "end": 259.11,
          "en": "and you can mention multiple things, not just one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 259.11,
          "end": 262.92,
          "en": "So, in the double quotes, you can mention application/json.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 262.92,
          "end": 265.29,
          "en": "Now, by doing this, what you're saying is, hey, you know,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 265.29,
          "end": 268.77,
          "en": "this particular method will only return the JSON data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 268.77,
          "end": 269.79,
          "en": "not XML.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 269.79,
          "end": 272.207,
          "en": "I mean, we are saying it'll only return JSON,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 272.207,
          "end": 274.65,
          "en": "we are not saying you're not going to return XML.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 274.65,
          "end": 275.88,
          "en": "Let's not talk about negative stuff.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 275.88,
          "end": 277.14,
          "en": "We can say positive stuff.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 277.14,
          "end": 278.55,
          "en": "What you want to return? JSON.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 278.55,
          "end": 280.44,
          "en": "But if you request for something else.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 280.44,
          "end": 282.06,
          "en": "If you go back here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 282.06,
          "end": 284.76,
          "en": "and you can see I'm still requesting for XML,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 284.76,
          "end": 285.65999999999997,
          "en": "click on Send.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 285.65999999999997,
          "end": 287.01,
          "en": "It'll not work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 287.01,
          "end": 289.29,
          "en": "It'll say Not Acceptable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 289.29,
          "end": 291.24,
          "en": "You got this status error, 406.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 291.24,
          "end": 292.756,
          "en": "But yeah, if you request for JSON,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
